{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"chilled-refutable-axisdeer","creation_channel":"python","description":"Scope: `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/**` (38 files) and `src/rebar/llm/workflow/**` (26 files). ~230 lines leave of 24,304 LOC — only 0.9%, because this subtree's prose is unusually load-bearing (fail-open/fail-closed contracts, byte-compat pins, patch-seam invariants).\n\n36 of 38 history blocks already cite a ticket id, so most of the work is 'reduce to the citation'. Only two are costly: untracked follow-ups in `production_batch_runner.py` that must be filed first.\n\nVerified stale: SIX sites say 'the deterministic floor (P1-P9)' while `DET_CHECKS` has 11 entries and `registry.CANONICAL_DET` runs P1..P11; `orchestrator.py:9` additionally misstates which checks block. `reuse.py:36-37` cites four line numbers, all four wrong.\n\nThree new ADRs: the unversioned additive-only attestation manifest; the Burr tripwire (a 4-condition adoption trigger list spread across three docstrings, with a test asserting the prose exists); gate context is never elided (including a WITHDRAWN alternative documented as a signed-false-PASS vector).\n\nBiggest headroom win: `workflow/executor.py` 791 -> ~769, almost entirely from three 'so this module stays under the module-size cap' notes.\n\nByte-pinned json.dumps rationale in attest.py/pass1.py is maintainer-blessed and must stay verbatim — converging it would invalidate live attestations.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every non-KEEP unit in scope is relocated or deleted per its destination\n- [ ] The shard's do_not_move list is appended to `.joe-janitor/tools.md` BEFORE any edit lands\n- [ ] Verified-stale comments are corrected where they document a live invariant, deleted only where obsolete\n- [ ] No load-bearing invariant is lost; measured-fact and anti-refactor warnings stay verbatim","id":"8b97-dc9e-37ba-45a8","parent_id":"c3d1-a642-4e1d-44b7","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Comment triage: plan_review and workflow"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788160779306022001,"uuid":"e97ba92b-e750-474f-a6c8-6c5a51535aee"}